ents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsuderman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-25T16:49:06Z","updated_at":"2023-09-25T16:49:06Z","body":"> Could this be related to the accuracy errors for larger batch sizes? #14601\r\n\r\nIt could be. There is a pretty easy way to check - we just need to disable concurrent execution.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1734122941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1773970546","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15007#issuecomment-1773970546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15007","id":1773970546,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5pvKRy","user":{"login":"jpienaar","id":706766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/706766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar","html_url":"https://github.com/jpienaar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jpienaar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-10-22T02:03:05Z","updated_at":"2023-10-22T02:03:05Z","body":"Skipping ScheduleConcurrency pass avoids the RNG failure, now I'm pretty sure that would decrease performance, but is that an option until this is triaged? (seems this would result in rather non-trivial numerical issues)\r\n\r\nI also don't quite understand how to see that this pass is doing the wrong thing in Rob's example, the output post pass is:\r\n\r\n```mlir\r\nmodule {\r\n  util.global private mutable @_constant__timepoint = #stream.timepoint<immediate> : !stream.timepoint\r\n  util.global private @_constant : !stream.resource<constant>\r\n  util.global private mutable @global_hlo_rng_state__timepoint = #stream.timepoint<immediate> : !stream.timepoint\r\n  util.global private mutable @global_hlo_rng_state : !stream.resource<variable>\r\n  func.func @rng_uniform_3d() -> (!hal.buffer_view, !hal.buffer_view) {\r\n    %c0 = arith.constant 0 : index\r\n    %c16 = arith.constant 16 : index\r\n    %c32 = arith.constant 32 : index\r\n    %global_hlo_rng_state__timepoint = util.global.load @global_hlo_rng_state__timepoint : !stream.timepoint\r\n    %global_hlo_rng_state = util.global.load @global_hlo_rng_state : !stream.resource<variable>\r\n    %_constant__timepoint = util.global.load @_constant__timepoint : !stream.timepoint\r\n    %_constant = util.global.load @_constant : !stream.resource<constant>\r\n    %0 = stream.timepoint.join max(%_constant__timepoint, %global_hlo_rng_state__timepoint) => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %c0_0 = arith.constant 0 : index\r\n    %1:3 = stream.resource.pack slices({\r\n      [0, 0] = %c32,\r\n      [0, 0] = %c32\r\n    }) : index\r\n    %result, %result_timepoint = stream.resource.alloca uninitialized await(%0) => !stream.resource<external>{%1#0} => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %2 = stream.resource.subview %result[%1#1] : !stream.resource<external>{%1#0} -> !stream.resource<external>{%c32}\r\n    %3 = stream.resource.subview %result[%1#2] : !stream.resource<external>{%1#0} -> !stream.resource<external>{%c32}\r\n    %4:3 = stream.resource.pack slices({\r\n      [1, 1] = %c32,\r\n      [0, 2] = %c32\r\n    }) : index\r\n    %result_1, %result_timepoint_2 = stream.resource.alloca uninitialized await(%0) => !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0} => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %5 = stream.timepoint.join max(%0, %result_timepoint, %result_timepoint_2) => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %6 = arith.addi %4#1, %c16 : index\r\n    %7 = stream.cmd.execute await(%5) => with(%_constant as %arg0: !stream.resource<constant>{%c32}, %global_hlo_rng_state as %arg1: !stream.resource<variable>{%c16}, %2 as %arg2: !stream.resource<external>{%c32}, %3 as %arg3: !stream.resource<external>{%c32}, %result_1 as %arg4: !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0}) {\r\n      stream.cmd.concurrent {\r\n        stream.cmd.dispatch @rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_0::@rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_0_generic_8_i32 {\r\n          ro %arg0[%c0 for %c32] : !stream.resource<constant>{%c32},\r\n          wo %arg2[%c0_0 for %c32] : !stream.resource<external>{%c32}\r\n        }\r\n        stream.cmd.dispatch @rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_1::@rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_1_generic_4_i32 {\r\n          ro %arg1[%c0 for %c16] : !stream.resource<variable>{%c16},\r\n          rw %arg4[%4#1 for %c16] : !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0},\r\n          ro %arg4[%6 for %c16] : !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0}\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n      stream.cmd.dispatch @rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_0::@rng_uniform_3d_dispatch_0_generic_8_i32 {\r\n        ro %arg4[%4#2 for %c32] : !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0},\r\n        wo %arg3[%c0_0 for %c32] : !stream.resource<external>{%c32}\r\n      }\r\n    } => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %8 = stream.resource.dealloca await(%7) => %result_1 : !stream.resource<transient>{%4#0} => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %9 = stream.timepoint.join max(%8, %7) => !stream.timepoint\r\n    %10:2 = stream.timepoint.await %9 => %2, %3 : !stream.resource<external>{%c32}, !stream.resource<external>{%c32}\r\n    %11 = stream.tensor.export %10#0 : tensor<2x2x2xi32> in !stream.resource<external>{%c32} -> !hal.buffer_view\r\n    %12 = stream.tensor.export %10#1 : tensor<2x2x2xi32> in !stream.resource<external>{%c32} -> !hal.buffer_view\r\n    return %11, %12 : !hal.buffer_view, !hal.buffer_view\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe last dispatch here reads from arg4 which is transient and writes to arg3 which is external, and arg4 was written to. So not sure how to see this is wrong (potentially a more general question about how one debug these, but hey we have a failure here to learn from :) )","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1773970546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1783457101","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15007#issuecomment-1783457101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15007","id":1783457101,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5qTWVN","user":{"login":"allieculp","id":60522369,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTIyMzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60522369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp","html_url":"https://github.com/allieculp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allieculp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_typ